// A hand-inlined subtype VALUE whose category disagrees with the loaded
// registry declaration of the same name: `Island` is declared a LAND type
// ([CR#205.3i] via the builtin `BasicLandType` row), so a value carrying
// `types: [Creature]` is a forgery, not a new subtype — the declaration is
// the [CR#205.3] authority. (The face carries both types so the
// [CR#205.3d] floor — which reads the DECLARED category — stays satisfied
// and only the category forgery trips.)
Normal(
  name: "Reject Forged Island Category",
  types: [Land, Creature],
  subtypes: [(name: "Island", types: [Creature])],
  power: 1,
  toughness: 1,
)
